Launch without taking the user's focus.

Applies to: tauri-runtime-cef 3.0.0-alpha.7, applied in vendor/tauri-runtime-cef.
Not offered upstream in this form (an environment switch); a builder option would be.

Why: winit activates the app when its event loop starts. An automated run (the smoke run,
the local-network probe) must not pull the user out of what they are doing, so with
`TAURI_CEF_NO_ACTIVATE` set the loop is built with `activate_ignoring_other_apps(false)`.
A normal launch does not set it.

diff --git a/src/runtime.rs b/src/runtime.rs
index 1a6d3f6c..bd998217 100644
--- a/src/runtime.rs
+++ b/src/runtime.rs
@@ -3350,6 +3350,12 @@ impl<T: UserEvent> CefRuntime<T> {
 
     #[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
     event_loop_builder.with_default_menu(false);
+    // Lets an automated run start without
+    // taking the user's focus. winit activates the app at launch otherwise.
+    #[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
+    if std::env::var_os("TAURI_CEF_NO_ACTIVATE").is_some() {
+      event_loop_builder.with_activate_ignoring_other_apps(false);
+    }
 
     let event_loop = event_loop_builder
       .build()
